start:configfirewall_sn_auto
description:The service node runs "configfirewall --auto" as a postbootscript. The case reads what the SN kept: firewalld running and enabled, the SN NIC to the CN in the trusted zone, which serves DHCP and NFS, and the marker of configfirewall. The kickstart of the SN disables the firewall, so an SN that does not run configfirewall --auto, or runs one that stops firewalld, has none of these
label:firewall
os:rhels
cmd:xdcp $$SN /opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall/fw_check.sh /tmp/fw_check.sh
check:rc==0
cmd:xdsh $$SN "/tmp/fw_check.sh check \$(/tmp/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__) 67/udp 69/udp 80/tcp 2049/tcp 3001/tcp 3002/tcp"
check:rc==0
check:output=~FWCHECK-OK
check:output!~FWCHECK-BAD
cmd:xdsh $$SN "firewall-cmd --get-zone-of-interface=\$(/tmp/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__)"
check:rc==0
check:output=~: trusted
cmd:xdsh $$SN "cat /etc/xcat/configfirewall.backend"
check:rc==0
check:output=~: firewalld
cmd:xdsh $$SN rm -f /tmp/fw_check.sh
end

start:configfirewall_xcatconfig_keeps
description:xcatconfig -i keeps the firewall that configfirewall configured on the MN. The case runs configfirewall, then xcatconfig -i, which stops and disables the firewall unless the configfirewall marker exists, and reads the firewall back. The case puts back the xCAT DB, the node host keys, the marker and the firewall state of the MN
label:firewall
os:rhels
cmd:/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall/fw_check.sh save
check:rc==0
cmd:rm -rf /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep && mkdir -p /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'if [ -e /etc/xcat/configfirewall.backend ]; then cp -p /etc/xcat/configfirewall.backend /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep/marker; fi'
check:rc==0
cmd:dumpxCATdb -p /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep/db
check:rc==0
cmd:cp -a /etc/xcat/hostkeys /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep/hostkeys && cp -a /install/postscripts/hostkeys /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep/pshostkeys
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; /install/postscripts/configfirewall --private "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__)" --public "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-default)"'
check:rc==0
cmd:xcatconfig -i
check:rc==0
check:output=~Keeping the firewall that configfirewall configured
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; $T/fw_check.sh check "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__)" 22/tcp 3001/tcp 3002/tcp 69/udp 67/udp 80/tcp 443/tcp 2049/tcp 873/tcp'
check:rc==0
check:output=~FWCHECK-OK
check:output!~FWCHECK-BAD
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; $T/fw_check.sh check "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-default)" 22/tcp 3001/tcp 3002/tcp 69/udp 80/tcp 443/tcp 873/tcp'
check:rc==0
check:output=~FWCHECK-OK
check:output!~FWCHECK-BAD
cmd:rm -rf /etc/xcat/hostkeys /install/postscripts/hostkeys && cp -a /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep/hostkeys /etc/xcat/hostkeys && cp -a /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep/pshostkeys /install/postscripts/hostkeys
check:rc==0
cmd:restorexCATdb -p /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep/db
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'if [ -e /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep/marker ]; then cp -p /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep/marker /etc/xcat/configfirewall.backend; else rm -f /etc/xcat/configfirewall.backend; fi'
check:rc==0
cmd:/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall/fw_check.sh restore
check:rc==0
cmd:rm -rf /tmp/xcattest-fwkeep
end

start:configfirewall_xcatprobe_xcatmn
description:xcatprobe xcatmn accepts the firewall that configfirewall configured on the MN. The probe sees a firewall when iptables lists a DROP rule, and firewalld on nftables lists none, so the case adds one DROP rule for the discard port 9/tcp. Without the configfirewall marker the probe must warn, which proves the rule arms the check. After configfirewall the firewall check must pass. The case puts back the marker and the firewall state of the MN
label:firewall
os:rhels
cmd:/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall/fw_check.sh save
check:rc==0
cmd:rm -rf /tmp/xcattest-fwprobe && mkdir -p /tmp/xcattest-fwprobe
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'if [ -e /etc/xcat/configfirewall.backend ]; then mv /etc/xcat/configfirewall.backend /tmp/xcattest-fwprobe/marker; fi'
check:rc==0
cmd:iptables -I INPUT -p tcp --dport 9 -j DROP
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; xcatprobe xcatmn -i "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__)" -H 2>&1'
check:output=~Checking firewall is disabled\.\.\..*\[WARN\]
check:output=~Firewall is configured on current server
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; /install/postscripts/configfirewall --private "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__)" --public "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-default)"'
check:rc==0
cmd:iptables -C INPUT -p tcp --dport 9 -j DROP
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; xcatprobe xcatmn -i "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__)" -H 2>&1'
check:output=~Checking firewall is disabled\.\.\..*\[ OK \]
check:output!~Firewall is configured on current server
cmd:iptables -D INPUT -p tcp --dport 9 -j DROP
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'if [ -e /tmp/xcattest-fwprobe/marker ]; then cp -p /tmp/xcattest-fwprobe/marker /etc/xcat/configfirewall.backend; else rm -f /etc/xcat/configfirewall.backend; fi'
check:rc==0
cmd:/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall/fw_check.sh restore
check:rc==0
cmd:rm -rf /tmp/xcattest-fwprobe
end

start:configfirewall_ipv6_run
description:Runs last on the IPv6 leaf, after the IPv6 discovery and provisioning cases. firewalld runs on the MN and entered the active state before the first xcattest run on this MN started, so firewalld ran through every case of the run without a stop. The MN NIC to the IPv6 address of the CN is in the trusted zone, which passes DHCPv6, ICMPv6 and router advertisements
label:firewall
os:rhels
cmd:firewall-cmd --state
check:rc==0
check:output=~^running
cmd:sh -c 'F=$(ls /opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/result/xcattest.log.* | sort | head -1); T=${F##*.}; S=$(date -d "${T:0:8} ${T:8:2}:${T:10:2}:${T:12:2}" +%s); A=$(date -d "$(systemctl show -p ActiveEnterTimestamp --value firewalld)" +%s); echo "firewalld active since $A, first xcattest run $T ($S)"; [ -n "$A" ] && [ -n "$S" ] && [ "$A" -lt "$S" ]'
check:rc==0
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; $T/fw_check.sh check "$($T/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__)" 547/udp 69/udp 80/tcp 2049/tcp 3001/tcp'
check:rc==0
check:output=~FWCHECK-OK
check:output!~FWCHECK-BAD
cmd:sh -c 'T=/opt/xcat/share/xcat/tools/autotest/testcase/configfirewall; firewall-cmd --get-zone-of-interface="$($T/fw_check.sh nic-to __GETNODEATTR($$CN,ip)__)"'
check:rc==0
check:output=~^trusted
end
